Problem

TopologyDescriptionFormatter (tools/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/tools/streams/TopologyDescriptionFormatter.java) labels global stores starting at {{{}topology.subtopologies().size(){}}}:
 
 {{int globalStoreId = topology.subtopologies().size();

for (final GlobalStore globalStore : topology.globalStores())

{ appendGlobalStore(sb, globalStore, globalStoreId++);}

}}
This assumes regular subtopologies are numbered {{{}0..N-1{}}}. In Kafka Streams, global stores and subtopologies share one node-group id counter ({{{}InternalTopologyBuilder{}}}), so if the app defines its global store/table first, the global store gets id 0 and regular subtopologies get {{{}1..N{}}}.
Example

Global store defined first, then two regular subtopologies (real ids 1, 2). CLI output:
 
 Sub-topology: 1Sub-topology: 2Sub-topology: 2 for global store (will not generate tasks) <- collides with real sub-topology 2
Stock Streams TopologyDescription.toString() would label the global store {{{}0{}}}.
Impact

Cosmetic, CLI display only (KIP-1331 {{{}-describe -topology{}}}). Stored/pushed topology data and the CRD are unaffected. Not a release blocker; can confuse operators reading the output.
Possible fixes
 # Minimal: start global labels at max(subtopology id) + 1 — removes the collision, but may still differ from Streams' own id.

 # Exact: carry the global store's real id in the KIP-1331 description and print it — matches stock Streams output, but needs a protocol/API change.

