             Summary: KafkaAdminClient calls MetricsReporter.close() twice during a single shutdown
                 Key: KAFKA-21369
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21369
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: clients, admin
    Affects Versions: 4.3.1, 4.0.0
            Reporter: Tycho Schottdorf


*Affected versions verified at runtime:* 4.0.0 and 4.3.1. Control: 3.9.0. The same shutdown paths are present in trunk.

h2. Description

A single call to {{Admin.close(Duration)}} invokes {{close()}} twice on the same configured {{MetricsReporter}} instance. The calls originate from the caller thread and the Admin client's network thread. A producer configured with the same counting reporter closes it once.

In Kafka 4.3.1, [KafkaAdminClient.close(Duration)|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.3.1/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/admin/KafkaAdminClient.java#L679] calls {{metrics.close()}}, and [AdminClientRunnable cleanup|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.3.1/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/admin/KafkaAdminClient.java#L1490] calls {{closeQuietly(metrics, "Metrics")}}. [Metrics.close()|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.3.1/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/metrics/Metrics.java#L674] invokes every reporter on each call without a closed-state guard.

This affects reporters that release shared resources. With Strimzi client-metrics-reporter 0.4.0, an Admin client releases the shared HTTP listener twice and can stop the endpoint while a producer remains open.

h2. Reproduction

Save the following as {{ReporterCloseCount.java}}. It uses Kafka classes only and does not require a broker or Strimzi's reporter. The Strimzi container supplies the exact tested Kafka client jar and Java runtime.

{code:java}
import java.time.Duration;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;
import org.apache.kafka.clients.admin.Admin;
import org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.KafkaProducer;
import org.apache.kafka.common.metrics.KafkaMetric;
import org.apache.kafka.common.metrics.MetricsReporter;
import org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer;
import org.apache.kafka.common.utils.AppInfoParser;

public class ReporterCloseCount {
    public static class Counting implements MetricsReporter {
        private final AtomicInteger closes = new AtomicInteger();
        private String clientId;
        public void configure(Map<String, ?> config) {
            clientId = config.get("client.id").toString();
        }
        public void init(List<KafkaMetric> metrics) { }
        public void metricChange(KafkaMetric metric) { }
        public void metricRemoval(KafkaMetric metric) { }
        public void close() {
            System.out.printf("%s reporter=%x close=%d thread=%s%n",
                clientId, System.identityHashCode(this), closes.incrementAndGet(),
                Thread.currentThread().getName());
        }
    }

    static Map<String, Object> config(String id) {
        return new HashMap<>(Map.of(
            "bootstrap.servers", "127.0.0.1:1",
            "client.id", id,
            "metric.reporters", Counting.class.getName()));
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(ReporterCloseCount.class.getClassLoader());
        System.out.println("Kafka " + AppInfoParser.getVersion());
        Map<String, Object> p = config("producer");
        p.put("key.serializer", StringSerializer.class.getName());
        p.put("value.serializer", StringSerializer.class.getName());
        KafkaProducer<String, String> producer = new KafkaProducer<>(p);
        producer.close(Duration.ofSeconds(5));
        Admin admin = Admin.create(config("admin"));
        admin.close(Duration.ofSeconds(5));
    }
}
{code}

{code:bash}
docker run --rm --network none --read-only --tmpfs /tmp:rw,nosuid,size=256m \
  -v "$PWD:/repro:ro" --entrypoint java \
  quay.io/strimzi/kafka:1.2.0-kafka-4.3.1@sha256:fef34b5438e8556cc08c01f3e254e47346f061b53a4e38d4289853777e0ea7f1 \
  -cp "/opt/kafka/libs/*" /repro/ReporterCloseCount.java
{code}

Relevant output with Kafka 4.3.1 and Java 21.0.12:

{noformat}
Kafka 4.3.1
producer reporter=28cb9120 close=1 thread=main
admin reporter=5e742e4 close=1 thread=main
admin reporter=5e742e4 close=2 thread=kafka-admin-client-thread | admin
{noformat}

The two Admin lines identify the same reporter instance. A separate version comparison using a counting reporter produced:

|| Kafka client version || Producer reporter close calls || Admin reporter close calls ||
| 3.9.0 | 1 | 1 |
| 4.0.0 | 1 | 2 |
| 4.3.1 | 1 | 2 |

h2. Expected behavior

Closing an Admin client once should close each owned reporter once. Repeated closure of its {{Metrics}} repository should not invoke reporter teardown again.

{{Metrics}} implements {{java.io.Closeable}}, whose [contract requires subsequent closes to have no effect|https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/io/Closeable.html]. {{MetricsReporter}} extends {{AutoCloseable}}, whose [contract does not require idempotence|https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/AutoCloseable.html].

h2. Regression and related work

The direct {{metrics.close()}} call was added in [commit 4ed0a958|https://github.com/apache/kafka/commit/4ed0a958e54ee6c3b80e4eb5fbc986e5b6be49e5] for [KAFKA-17248|https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17248], released in Kafka 4.0.0. The [original review discussion|https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/17021#discussion_r1759041707] records that addition.

[KAFKA-19504|https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19504] concerns duplicate reporter construction and leaked unused instances. This report concerns repeated closure of the same instance and reproduces on 4.3.1 after that fix.

[Strimzi metrics-reporter #144|https://github.com/strimzi/metrics-reporter/issues/144] records the concrete shared-listener failure.

h2. Possible resolution

Ensure reporters are torn down only once during Admin shutdown, either by correcting shutdown ownership in {{KafkaAdminClient}} or by making {{Metrics.close()}} idempotent. A regression test should count calls to a custom reporter during a single Admin close and cover shutdown from both threads.




