A new optional field "initial_offsets"  will be added to the request body format for the POST /connectors endpoint. The value for this field has to adhere to format specified in KIP-875 else a 400 Bad Request response will be returned.
If the field is omitted in the request body, the current behaviour of creating connectors will be preserved. An example request body would look like:
CreateConnectorRequest
{
    "name": "file-src-1",
    "config": {
        "connector.class": "org.apache.kafka.connect.file.FileStreamSourceConnector",
        "file": "test.txt",
        "topic": "test-topic",
        "tasks.max": "1"
    },
    "initial_offsets": [
    {
      "partition": {
        //  source partition
      },
      "offset": {
        // Desired initial offset
      }
    }
  ]
}
As mentioned in  , the response message (`offsets_status`) for successfully setting the initial_offsets will depend on whether the connector has implemented alterOffsets()  method. If initial_offsets is missing from request, offsets_status  will not be present in the response.
If the connector has implemented alterOffsets  and everything has succeeded, the HTTP status will be 201 and the create-connector response body will be:
 response (definite success)
{
   "name": "ConnectorOne",
    "config": {...},
  "offsets_status": "The offsets for this connector have been set successfully"
}
If the connector has not implemented alterOffsets  but everything else has succeeded, the HTTP status will be 201 and the create-connector response body will be:
response (possible success)
{
   "name": "ConnectorOne",
    "config": {...},
  "offsets_status": "The framework-managed offsets for this connector have been set successfully. However, if this connector manages offsets externally, they will need to be manually set in the system that the connector uses."
}
