The encoded long is a signed count of nanoseconds since the Unix epoch; negative values represent instants before 1970 and round-trip exactly (same reasoning as TimestampMicros):
 static long fromLogical(Schema schema, Instant value) {
     // schema name check ...
     return Math.addExact(
